rum of diseases. The company offers hepatic-targeted programs, including Agazisiran, a complement factor B (CFB) program that represents a pipeline-in-a-product opportunity, where a single therapeutic candidate has the potential to address multiple indications; Onvuzosiran, a clinical program for the prevention of HAE attacks; and ADX-626, a Factor XI (FXI) program for secondary stroke prevention with additional clinical potential for stroke prevention in atrial fibrillation. It also offers extrahepatic-targeted programs, such as ADX-077, an adipose-targeted obesity program designed to reduce body weight and fat while preserving lean mass; and ADX-199, a neuron-targeted program designed to selectively silence and degrade amyloid-\u00df precursor protein (APP) mRNA in neurons, which is genetically linked to Alzheimer's disease. The company was incorporated in 2019 and is based in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Li  Zhen Ph.D. | Co-Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $875,405 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 100 people. Revenue per employee of $34K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $2.6M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $61K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 25\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). R&D investment of 2073% of revenue (heavy) signals commitment to product development and talent. Note: heavy R&D investment has not yet translated to above-average workforce productivity \u2014 watch for commercialisation lag.","financial_summary":["ADARx Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.6B market cap on $3M of annual revenue.","The business throws off $259M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7520 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 178% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 42% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"SGA costs surged 36% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 2562% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 82% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 194% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $87.7M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","R&D investment (2073% of revenue) is above Healthcare peers, supporting innovation","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ADARx Pharmaceuticals (NASDAQ:ADRX) Posts Quarterly Earnings Results, Misses Expectations By $1.34 EPS","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/adarx-pharmaceuticals-nasdaqadrx-posts-quarterly-earnings-results-misses-expectations-by-1-34-eps.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794521455.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"ADARx Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (NASDAQ:ADRX) Stock Short Interest Rises 63.6%","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/03/adarx-pharmaceuticals-inc-nasdaqadrx-stock-short-interest-rises-63-6.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793704868.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.969,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ADARx Pharmaceuticals to Present at the UBS Global Biopharma Conference","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/adarx-pharmaceuticals-present-ubs-global-130000716.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794229200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ADARx Reports Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Provides Business Updates","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/adarx-reports-third-quarter-2026-210500454.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794517500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.273,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"This Restaurant Brands Analyst Begins Coverage On A Bullish Note; Here Are Top 5 Initiations